# Gates

Gates are a first-class deliverable — not ad-hoc shell scripts.

## Bundled gates

- Shell: `src/shipgate/catalog/bundled/gates/` + configs in `configs/gates/`
- Python helpers: `src/shipgate/gates/` and `src/shipgate/policy/` — never inline heredocs in shell gates
- Emit JSON to `SHIPGATE_REPORT`; shell helpers in `lib.sh` (`gate_init`, `gate_fail`, `gate_finish`)

## Project gates

- Scaffold: `shipgate gates init <name>` → `.shipgate/gates/<name>.sh`
- Discovered at runtime into the `local-gates` suite
- `policy` suite = bundled gates; `local-gates` = project-discovered gates

## Rules

- Gates must be deterministic and scoped to the project target
- Reuse `lib.sh` and Python modules — do not duplicate finding JSON shape
- New bundled gates need catalog tool YAML + config + normalizer (`gate_json` or dedicated)
